00:29:45.000 --> 00:29:45.500
So, okay.

00:29:46.860 --> 00:29:49.380
I'll take the gentleman
back there on stand, right?

00:29:49.380 --> 00:29:50.820
Yes, yes, go ahead.

00:29:50.820 --> 00:29:52.020
- I'll speak up loud.
- Okay.

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:53.745
- Mishal Kapoor, you talked a lot

00:29:53.745 --> 00:29:55.261
about AI and its productivity

00:29:55.261 --> 00:29:57.300
and its role in digital transformation.

00:29:57.300 --> 00:30:01.560
What is your opinion on blockchain?

00:30:01.560 --> 00:30:06.478
The technology rather than the news?

00:30:06.478 --> 00:30:10.560
- Look, I mean, I'm neutral to it, right?

00:30:10.560 --> 00:30:14.700
Which is it's a technology
that has a set of use cases

00:30:14.700 --> 00:30:16.380
and we support it today.

00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:21.360
And even a distributed
database is a good thing.

00:30:22.020 --> 00:30:23.160
It has its users.

00:30:23.160 --> 00:30:27.780
I think the entirety of that
space we have not yet found,

00:30:27.780 --> 00:30:30.660
like in the context the
difference between, I would say,

00:30:30.660 --> 00:30:34.980
all this Web3 and AI and
quite frankly even Metaverse

00:30:34.980 --> 00:30:38.880
is all of these three things
are all going to happen,

00:30:38.880 --> 00:30:42.060
but you need to have the killer apps.

00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:45.060
What is the use case
that gets broad adoption?

00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:49.260
What's the Chat GPT moment on blockchain?

00:30:50.520 --> 00:30:53.400
When I first sort of had, you know,

00:30:53.400 --> 00:30:55.860
got to know the web, it
was through, you know,

00:30:55.860 --> 00:31:00.000
the Mosaic browser, I think
all of us remember like,

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.800
I think at least the difficulty I have

00:31:01.800 --> 00:31:03.900
in some of these other
technologies, what's the moment?

00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:06.120
Like even on the metaverse,
that's why I'm very, very keen

00:31:06.120 --> 00:31:08.220
even at WEF we are, you know,

00:31:08.220 --> 00:31:11.160
the Global Collaboration Village and Mesh.

00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:12.720
That's the stuff, right?

00:31:12.720 --> 00:31:14.100
Which is, if we can start saying, hey,

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:16.320
this is just the next
generation of presence,

00:31:16.320 --> 00:31:20.100
here is how teams will evolve
to include more presence

00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:22.500
and then we are all using
it and it's mainstream,

00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:24.480
then we'll know that moment has arrived.

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:25.740
So I think we have to keep pushing,

00:31:25.740 --> 00:31:28.080
I believe in all of these
technologies and it's up to us

00:31:28.080 --> 00:31:30.840
on the technology side to make
it more real for more people.

